<newsitem itemid="406982" id="root" date="1997-02-27" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: KWV lifts half yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>KWV lifts half yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     115.9	 vs 93.1</p>
<p>    Interim div (cts)	28	   vs 23</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    48.69	vs 39.09</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    11.75	vs  9.63</p>
<p>    Tax			   0.005     vs  0.005</p>
<p>    Interest received	 0.023     vs  0.013</p>
<p>    Equity earnings	  36.95	vs 29.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		   11.76	vs  9.66</p>
<p>Div declared Feb 10, payable March 7</p>
<p>on register Feb 28</p>
<p>Full name: KWV Investments Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that although private consumer spending growth was falling, it expected profit growth to be maintained for the full year.</p>
<p>The only assets of KWV Investments Ltd is a 30 percent share in both Distillers Corp Ltd and Stellenbosch Farmers' Winery Ltd, which is held through Rembrandt-KWV Investments Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
